From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] nss_qdisc: drop the never-set classify-offload skip

skb_skip_tc_classify_offload() tests an sk_buff bit that only the QSDK
IFB driver sets. The kernel here never sets it, so the test is always
false; the bit and its helpers are gone from the kernel.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc.c
+++ b/nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc.c
@@ -1219,14 +1219,6 @@ extern int nss_qdisc_enqueue(struct sk_b
 		return NET_XMIT_SUCCESS;
 	}
 
-	/*
-	 * Skip the shaping of already shaped packets.
-	 */
-	if (skb_skip_tc_classify_offload(skb)) {
-		nss_qdisc_mark_and_schedule(nq->qdisc, skb);
-		return NET_XMIT_SUCCESS;
-	}
-
 	if (!nq->is_virtual) {
 		/*
 		 * TX to an NSS physical - the shaping will occur as part of normal
